{
  "about": "Canonical JSON for argsHash: the Go canonjson package and the runtime's canonicalJson must give these exact bytes. argsHash is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the canonical UTF-8 bytes. input is JSON text; a vector with error true must be refused.",
  "normalForm": [
    "object keys sorted by Unicode code point (UTF-8 byte order), not UTF-16 code units",
    "no whitespace; a duplicate key keeps its last value",
    "strings: \\\", \\\\, \\b, \\f, \\n, \\r, \\t, other U+0000-U+001F as \\u00xx (lowercase hex), U+2028 and U+2029 as \\u2028 and \\u2029; everything else raw UTF-8, including < > & / and U+007F",
    "a lone surrogate becomes U+FFFD",
    "numbers as IEEE 754 doubles in the shortest round-trip form; exponent form at 1e21 and above and below 1e-6 (1e+21, 1e-7); an integer above 2^53 rounds like a double",
    "negative zero is 0",
    "a number outside the double range (1e400) is refused"
  ],
